            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "i assume you mean https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2493 , and if so : \n\n> I don't want users to have to manually set some `vim.g` variables separately from enabling 'mini.files', which can be and usually is loaded lazily (i.e. after startup).\n\nthat's definitely a fair expectation. \n\nthe discomfort is that somehow, we need a way for a plugin to declare that it \"owns\" presentation of directory bufs. historically with netrw, that was achieved by [deleting the augroups of competitors](https://github.com/justinmk/vim-dirvish/blob/4cbf39ce024c57f700c4d5502cc172ea91d69360/plugin/dirvish.vim#L22-L24).\n\ni've lost track of why we can't support that with dir.lua, but i think it's because of my hope/insistence on using `filetype=directory` \"somehow\" as the central interface for deciding dir-buffer presentation.\n\nwould it make sense to (1) support the augroup hack, and (2) also keep the `filetype=directory` stuff we've done? so that buys time without regressing anything.",
