            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> ... the discomfort is that somehow, we need a way for a plugin to declare that it \"owns\" presentation of directory bufs. historically with netrw, that was achieved by [deleting the augroups of competitors](https://github.com/justinmk/vim-dirvish/blob/4cbf39ce024c57f700c4d5502cc172ea91d69360/plugin/dirvish.vim#L22-L24)...\n\nIs a dedicated function worth considering? Something like: `require('nvim.dir').disown()`, providing an alternative for `augroup` deletion.\nA plugin could [call](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/4171fba613b64ade9a28e198bd5b4fea5ba45e22/lua/mini/files.lua#L1372) that function at any moment, dynamically taking ownership of the presentation of directory buffers.\n\nThat way, the plugin does not need to know how `nvim.dir` internally goes about 'disowning'.\n\nThe proposed [alternative](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2493#issuecomment-4948174358) using an autocommand with `filetype=directory` has a limitation: The plugin cannot invoke its **own** code using `vim.schedule`...\n\n",
