            "body": "> 3P dir browsers can:\n> \n>     1. delete the `nvim.dir` augroup\n> \n>     2. handle `FileType directory`\n\nThat's what I expected `dir.lua` to do from the start and what sounds like a solid approach.\n\n> what am i missing? (in one sentence, not a paragraph please)\n\nDeleting `nvim.dir` augroup disables `dir.lua` for the whole duration of the current session. It can be improved by another convention, but will probably not be needed by many.",
