            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> what am i missing?\n\nI haven't heard an argument/example of exactly _why_ deleting an autocmd is a desirable pattern besides a) it being done _one_ time upstream with FileExplorer and b) it existing in this one case to allow behavior that can/is enabled by a more idiomatic \"nvim\"-like pattern (autocmd + vim.b).\n\nAnyway, thanks for the commentary y'all, path seems clear ahead.",
